Using the **code_compiler** capabilities, we structure the engine to calculate forces. For any celestial body, the total gravitational force is the superposition of all forces exerted by other bodies in the system.

The multi-body gravitational calculations peak at realistic force calculations when we define the baseline constant as the universal gravitational constant. We must ensure that the continuous time-step integration used to update positions handles the stability of orbits, where small perturbations do not lead to catastrophic orbital decay, which is a common issue with weaker force models.

